  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ODA Programmes within MRC Centre for Virus Research</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Research and development activity contributing to the UK&#x2019;s strategy to address key development challenges.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The MRC-University of Glasgow Centre for Virus Research (CVR) is home to an internationally leading critical mass of virologists, entirely focused on the study of human viral diseases and viruses at the human-animal interface. Established in 2010 as a partnership between the University and the Medical Research Council (MRC), the CVR contributes to national virology capability and supports the global response to viruses and the diseases they cause.</narrative>
  </description>
